WEBVTT

00:39.874 --> 00:41.500
What is the cost of lies?

00:43.544 --> 00:45.588
It's not that we'll mistake them
for the truth.

00:46.464 --> 00:49.300
The real danger is that
if we hear enough lies,

00:50.301 --> 00:53.012
then we no longerrecognize
the truth at all.

00:54.722 --> 00:56.015
What can we do then?

00:56.724 --> 00:59.602
What else is left but to abandon
even the hope of truth

00:59.685 --> 01:03.397
and content ourselves instead
with stories?

01:04.357 --> 01:07.401
In these stories,
it doesn't matter hwo the heroes are.

01:08.152 --> 01:10.446
All we want to know is,
who is to blame?

01:11.697 --> 01:15.785
In this story, it was Anatoly Dyatlov.
He was the best choice.

01:16.452 --> 01:19.580
An arrogant, unpleasant man,
he ran the room that night.

01:19.664 --> 01:20.957
He gave the orders.

01:21.624 --> 01:22.708
And no friends.

01:23.751 --> 01:26.504
Or, at least, not important ones.

01:28.923 --> 01:33.594
And now, Dyatlov will spend the next
10 years in a prison labor camp.

01:34.845 --> 01:37.473
Of course, that sentence
is doubly unfair.

01:39.767 --> 01:42.436
There were far greater criminals
than him at work.

01:45.189 --> 01:47.316
And as for what Dyatlov did do...

01:47.984 --> 01:49.902
The man doesn't deserve prison.

01:51.696 --> 01:53.030
He deserves death.

02:07.420 --> 02:10.840
But instead, ten years
for "criminal mismanagement."

02:12.300 --> 02:13.342
What does that mean?

02:14.427 --> 02:15.511
No one knows.

02:16.470 --> 02:17.596
It doesn't matter.

02:20.308 --> 02:22.018
What does matter is that, to them,

02:23.853 --> 02:25.313
justice was done.

02:26.230 --> 02:28.941
Because, you see, to them,

02:29.859 --> 02:32.862
a just world is a sane world.

02:36.073 --> 02:38.409
There was nothing sane
about Chernobyl.

02:40.870 --> 02:42.621
What happened there,
what happened after,

02:42.997 --> 02:46.125
even the good we did, all of it...

02:47.877 --> 02:48.878
All of it...

02:50.713 --> 02:51.714
Madness.

02:56.385 --> 03:00.181
Well, I've given you
everything I know.

03:02.850 --> 03:04.518
They'll deny it, of course.

03:05.311 --> 03:06.437
They always do.

03:12.568 --> 03:13.861
I know you'll try your best.

07:38.250 --> 07:39.251
Lyudmilla?

08:04.693 --> 08:05.986
Comrade Dyatlov!

08:10.574 --> 08:14.078
Comrade Dyatlov! Comrade Dyatlov!

08:18.999 --> 08:21.835
Comrade Dyatlov! Comrade Dyatlov!

08:22.836 --> 08:23.921
What just happened?

08:24.755 --> 08:25.756
I don't know.

08:27.800 --> 08:28.926
There's a fire in the turbine hall.

08:31.512 --> 08:32.846
The turbine hall?

08:34.139 --> 08:36.266
The control system tank. Hydrogen.

08:37.267 --> 08:39.144
You and Toptunov,
you morons blew the tank.

08:39.561 --> 08:41.397
- No, that's not...
- This is an emergency.

08:41.480 --> 08:43.524
Everyone stay calm.
Our first priority is...

08:43.607 --> 08:44.650
- It's exploded!
- We know.

08:45.025 --> 08:46.485
Akimov, are we cooling
the reactor core?

08:46.568 --> 08:48.320
We shut it down,
but the control rods are still active.

08:48.987 --> 08:50.322
They're not all the way in.
I disengaged...

08:50.406 --> 08:52.991
All right. Try and disconnect
the servos from the standby console.

08:53.200 --> 08:54.451
You two, get the backup pumps running.

08:54.535 --> 08:56.328
We need water moving through the core.

08:56.412 --> 08:58.414
- That is all that matters.
- There is no core.

08:59.790 --> 09:01.458
It exploded! The core exploded.

09:05.254 --> 09:07.089
He's in shock. Get him out of here.

09:07.464 --> 09:08.590
The lid is off.

09:08.799 --> 09:10.676
The stack is burning. I saw it.

09:10.759 --> 09:13.554
You're confused.
RBMK reactor cores don't explode.

09:13.637 --> 09:15.013
- Akimov...
- Sasha.

09:15.097 --> 09:18.308
Don't worry, we did everything right.
Something strange has happened.

09:18.392 --> 09:19.685
- Do you taste metal?
- Akimov!

09:21.061 --> 09:23.522
Comrade Perevozchenko, what you're
saying is physically impossible.

09:23.605 --> 09:26.316
The core can't explode.
It has to be the tank.

09:28.026 --> 09:29.403
We're wasting time. Let's go.

09:29.778 --> 09:32.156
Get the hydrogen out of the generators
and pump water into the core.

09:32.656 --> 09:33.866
What about the fire?

09:34.783 --> 09:35.993
Call the fire brigade.

10:38.597 --> 10:40.599
- Is this Military Fire Station 2?
- Yes.

10:41.016 --> 10:42.392
What's happening with the accident?

10:42.476 --> 10:46.271
Explosion in the main building
between the third and fourth blocks.

10:47.773 --> 10:49.691
- Are there people there?
- Yes.

10:49.942 --> 10:51.276
Wake up the bosses. Call them.

10:52.152 --> 10:54.071
I already called mine.

10:54.154 --> 10:58.492
Wake them up, wake them up.
Wake up the entire officers' block.

11:00.536 --> 11:02.538
- Fire department.
- Hello, Ivankov?

11:02.663 --> 11:05.457
- Yes. Yes?
- You've been called to Pripyat.

11:05.624 --> 11:07.334
- Hello?
- Yes. Yes I can hear you.

11:07.417 --> 11:11.004
At the nuclear plant over there,
in the third and fourth blocks.

11:11.088 --> 11:12.130
The roof is on fire.

11:13.006 --> 11:14.550
You're not on call tonight.

11:14.633 --> 11:16.635
They're bringing everybody in,
military and civil.

11:17.344 --> 11:20.222
Pripyat, Polesskoe, Kiev.

11:21.098 --> 11:22.099
This is a big one.

11:23.684 --> 11:26.520
But it doesn't look right, the color.

11:26.812 --> 11:29.940
Pravik says he thinks they're shining
floodlights or something.

11:30.023 --> 11:31.400
And what if there are chemicals?

11:32.192 --> 11:33.610
"Chemicals"?

11:34.778 --> 11:35.988
The problem's the roof.

11:36.488 --> 11:37.531
It's covered in tar,

11:37.614 --> 11:40.450
so it's gonna burn all night,
and it'll stink like hell.

11:40.951 --> 11:43.328
That's it. That's the worst of it.

11:45.956 --> 11:46.957
Go back to bed.

12:22.951 --> 12:25.203
- Is it war?
- Where's the dosimeter?

12:25.954 --> 12:28.332
Here. Here.

12:35.047 --> 12:36.465
Are they bombing?

12:39.676 --> 12:42.262
What the fuck is this?
It's 3.6 roentgen.

12:42.346 --> 12:44.806
That's as high as it goes.
The good one's locked in a safe.

12:44.890 --> 12:46.224
I don't have a key.

12:46.892 --> 12:50.187
Valera... Your face.

12:52.397 --> 12:53.398
Come on.

12:54.107 --> 12:56.360
I'm going to find Khodemchuk
in the pump room.

12:56.443 --> 12:57.945
You, here.

12:58.570 --> 13:01.949
Get Shashenok. He's in 604. Go.

13:02.366 --> 13:03.784
We need to get everyone out!

13:17.673 --> 13:18.674
Shit.

13:18.757 --> 13:21.051
Hey! We need to get
to the reactor hall.

13:21.134 --> 13:24.054
- The lift's destroyed.
- Up two flights and across.

13:24.513 --> 13:26.974
- Right.
- Why are you going there?

13:47.119 --> 13:48.328
Have you seen Khodemchuk?

13:48.954 --> 13:51.248
- No. Where's Viktor?
- Still in the pump room.

13:54.418 --> 13:55.585
Stay here. I'll come back.

13:58.588 --> 13:59.965
Viktor!

14:17.983 --> 14:19.526
Viktor.

14:21.111 --> 14:22.112
Viktor.

14:22.904 --> 14:23.905
Oh!

14:24.156 --> 14:26.491
Viktor, I'm gonna get you out of here.

14:27.159 --> 14:28.910
Can you stand?

14:29.870 --> 14:31.038
Khodemchuk...

14:31.121 --> 14:32.205
Where?

14:35.250 --> 14:36.626
Get Khodemchuk.

15:20.670 --> 15:22.589
I dropped the control rods
from the other panel.

15:22.672 --> 15:24.466
- They're still up.
- What?

15:24.549 --> 15:26.676
They're still only a third
of the way in. I don't know why.

15:27.135 --> 15:28.178
I already sent the trainees down

15:28.261 --> 15:29.596
to the reactor hall
to lower them by hand.

15:29.679 --> 15:31.598
- What about the pumps?
- I can't get through to Khodemchuk.

15:31.681 --> 15:34.226
- The lines are down.
- Fuck the phones and fuck Khodemchuk.

15:34.392 --> 15:35.894
- Are the pumps on or not?
- Stolyarchuk?

15:35.977 --> 15:38.772
My control panel's not working.
I tried calling for the electricians.

15:38.855 --> 15:42.567
I don't give a shit about the panel!
I need water in my reactor core!

15:43.610 --> 15:45.487
Get down there
and make sure those pumps are on.

15:46.822 --> 15:47.823
Now!

15:55.330 --> 15:57.082
What does the dosimeter say?

15:57.290 --> 15:59.543
Uh, 3.6 roentgen, but that's as high
as the meter...

15:59.626 --> 16:01.878
Three point six.
Not great, not terrible.

16:10.470 --> 16:11.680
We did everything right.

16:56.850 --> 16:58.435
You, connect those hooks!

17:04.566 --> 17:05.567
Get the pumps going!

17:05.650 --> 17:07.777
Yeah, over here!
I'm right with you!

17:11.823 --> 17:14.534
We're working
bottom to top. Go in fast.

17:35.513 --> 17:36.514
Vasily...

17:38.683 --> 17:41.311
- Hey, Vasily, what's this?
- I don't know, Misha.

17:41.394 --> 17:43.521
Don't fuck around with it.
Hook these up. Come on.

17:49.736 --> 17:50.737
Do you taste metal?

17:51.238 --> 17:53.949
- Yeah, what is that?
- I don't know.

17:55.992 --> 17:57.410
The valves, Misha.
The valves! Let's go.

17:57.619 --> 17:58.954
The valves! Come on!

18:31.444 --> 18:32.445
What do you need?

18:33.488 --> 18:35.156
We need to get into the reactor hall

18:35.240 --> 18:37.158
to lower the control rods,
but the door's jammed.

18:39.202 --> 18:40.787
I don't think there are control rods.

18:41.079 --> 18:42.247
I don't think there's a core.

18:44.541 --> 18:46.167
No, you're... You're mistaken.

18:47.377 --> 18:48.378
Akimov said.

19:05.937 --> 19:06.938
Let's go.

19:20.660 --> 19:22.203
No!

19:23.955 --> 19:25.915
Ignatenko, get on his hose!

19:26.624 --> 19:27.876
It's all right. Breathe.

19:28.209 --> 19:29.210
Misha.

19:29.878 --> 19:31.463
All right, all right.
Easy, Misha.

20:08.708 --> 20:09.709
Are you sure?

20:11.878 --> 20:12.879
Akimov...

20:26.851 --> 20:27.852
Move.

20:38.363 --> 20:39.739
Come on! Go! Go!

20:43.576 --> 20:44.869
Go! Go fast, go!

21:18.653 --> 21:19.654
Let's go!

21:20.864 --> 21:21.865
Let's go!

21:23.616 --> 21:25.326
Hey!

21:31.958 --> 21:32.959
Hey!

21:53.480 --> 21:55.607
Lyudmilla! Do you want
to come with us?

21:56.149 --> 21:57.150
Come where?

21:57.275 --> 21:59.068
We're going to the railroad bridge
to get a better look.

21:59.527 --> 22:01.863
It's not like anyone
can sleep with all the sirens.

22:02.113 --> 22:04.157
I don't think you should go.
It could be dangerous.

22:04.240 --> 22:05.241
What do you mean,
"dangerous"?

22:05.700 --> 22:07.202
It's a fire.
It's over there, we're over here.

22:07.285 --> 22:08.870
- Mikhail.
- What?

22:10.413 --> 22:12.457
Oh. Sorry.

22:17.462 --> 22:18.922
- Is Vasily...
- Yeah.

22:19.756 --> 22:21.132
Did he say it was bad?

22:21.216 --> 22:23.092
No. No, he said it was just the roof.

22:23.176 --> 22:25.553
Well, he's never gotten hurt before.
None of the boys have.

22:27.222 --> 22:28.223
He'll be fine.

22:29.974 --> 22:30.975
Get some rest.

22:43.947 --> 22:45.240
The tank, it's big enough.

22:45.323 --> 22:48.117
This kind of explosion,
the control tank on 71,

22:48.201 --> 22:49.452
it's 100 cubic meters.

22:49.536 --> 22:50.954
One hundred and ten.

22:51.120 --> 22:54.541
Hundred and ten.
It could do this, definitely.

22:55.083 --> 22:56.125
It's gone.

22:57.252 --> 22:58.503
I looked right into it.

22:59.379 --> 23:00.922
I looked into the core.

23:02.215 --> 23:04.050
Did you lower the control rods or not?

23:07.512 --> 23:08.846
Take him to the infirmary.

23:11.432 --> 23:13.017
Toptunov, take him!

23:16.563 --> 23:17.981
Where's Kudryavstev?

23:18.898 --> 23:20.024
He fell.

23:20.400 --> 23:22.986
- I need a medic! Anyone!
- He's delusional.

23:24.153 --> 23:25.905
- His face...
- Ruptured condenser lines.

23:25.989 --> 23:29.117
The feedwater is mildly contaminated.
He'll be fine. I've seen worse.

23:29.784 --> 23:31.995
Do we still have
a phone line to the outside?

23:33.913 --> 23:35.582
Akimov?

23:37.000 --> 23:38.334
Call in the day shift.

23:39.752 --> 23:40.795
But if the...

23:40.878 --> 23:42.630
We have to keep water flowing
into the core.

23:42.714 --> 23:45.550
We need electricians,
mechanics, we need bodies.

23:46.509 --> 23:48.386
How many times do I have to say it?

23:57.145 --> 23:59.272
I'm going to
the Administration Building now

23:59.355 --> 24:01.232
to call Bryukhanov and Fomin.

24:01.983 --> 24:03.192
They're gonna want a full report.

24:05.445 --> 24:07.989
Now, I don't know if I can
make things better for you...

24:09.282 --> 24:10.908
But I can certainly make them worse.

24:14.120 --> 24:16.372
Call in the day shift, Comrade Akimov.

24:20.168 --> 24:21.502
Yes, Comrade Dyatlov.

24:55.161 --> 24:56.162
You're doing fine.

24:57.580 --> 24:58.581
Raise her up.

25:02.835 --> 25:05.797
That one, maybe an hour.
This one, not until morning.

25:08.758 --> 25:10.301
How's it downstairs, Doctor?

25:10.968 --> 25:11.969
Quiet.

25:12.762 --> 25:13.888
Always is.

25:14.597 --> 25:16.599
Nothing at this hour but babies.

25:18.226 --> 25:20.603
Do you know I once went
two days without sleep?

25:21.229 --> 25:23.564
Ten women went into labor
at the same time.

25:23.898 --> 25:26.067
- Did I ever tell you that story?
- Yes.

25:28.361 --> 25:30.279
Well, I won't need you
in here for a while.

25:30.363 --> 25:32.782
If you want,
get some rest in the break room.

25:33.866 --> 25:35.702
They haven't brought
anyone in from the fire.

25:36.202 --> 25:37.245
What fire?

25:37.578 --> 25:38.830
The power plant.

25:40.248 --> 25:42.750
Oh.
Well, then it mustn't be too bad.

25:44.001 --> 25:45.294
Do we stock iodine?

25:45.837 --> 25:47.755
- Hmm?
- Iodine.

25:49.215 --> 25:50.633
You mean disinfectant?

25:50.717 --> 25:53.302
No, pills. Does the hospital
stock iodine pills?

25:53.386 --> 25:56.055
Iodine pills?
Why would we have iodine pills?

26:08.776 --> 26:10.153
Hello?

26:11.696 --> 26:12.697
Hello?

26:20.246 --> 26:21.664
Who else knows this?

26:24.167 --> 26:25.168
Have you called Fomin?

26:26.961 --> 26:31.132
Of course, I want you to call him.
If I'm up, he's up.

27:09.670 --> 27:12.924
Whatever the cause, the important
thing is that neither you nor I...

27:54.549 --> 27:56.551
I take it the safety test
was a failure.

27:56.968 --> 27:59.595
- We have the situation under control.
- "Under control"?

28:00.096 --> 28:01.430
It doesn't look
like it's under control.

28:01.514 --> 28:02.515
Shut up, Fomin.

28:04.100 --> 28:06.769
I have to tell the Central Committee
about this. Do you realize that?

28:07.228 --> 28:08.896
I have to get on the phone
and tell Maryin,

28:08.980 --> 28:12.441
or, God forbid, Frolyshev,
that my power plant is on fire.

28:12.525 --> 28:14.944
No one can blame you for this,
Director Bryukhanov.

28:15.027 --> 28:16.445
Of course no one can
blame me for this.

28:16.529 --> 28:19.657
How can I be responsible?
I was sleeping.

28:20.700 --> 28:22.618
Tell me what happened, quickly.

28:24.579 --> 28:27.748
We ran the test exactly as
Chief Engineer Fomin approved.

28:28.291 --> 28:31.002
Unit Shift Chief Akimov
and Engineer Toptunov

28:31.294 --> 28:32.920
encountered technical difficulties,

28:33.004 --> 28:36.257
leading to an accumulation of hydrogen
in the control system tank.

28:37.174 --> 28:38.634
It regrettably ignited,

28:38.718 --> 28:40.845
damaging the plant,
setting the roof on fire.

28:43.389 --> 28:44.765
The tank is quite large.

28:45.516 --> 28:47.143
It's the only logical explanation.

28:47.727 --> 28:51.022
Of course,
Deputy Chief Engineer Dyatlov

28:51.105 --> 28:55.026
was directly supervising the test,
so he would know best.

28:55.109 --> 28:56.986
A hydrogen tank, fire...

28:59.864 --> 29:01.657
- Reactor?
- We're taking measures to ensure

29:01.949 --> 29:03.701
a steady flow of water
through the core.

29:04.619 --> 29:07.413
- What about radiation?
- Obviously, down here it's nothing,

29:07.496 --> 29:11.584
but in the reactor building,
I'm being told, 3.6 roentgen per hour.

29:12.501 --> 29:14.211
Well, that's not great,
but it's not horrifying.

29:14.295 --> 29:15.296
Not at all.

29:16.047 --> 29:17.757
From the feedwater, I assume.

29:17.840 --> 29:18.841
Mmm-hmm.

29:20.593 --> 29:23.596
We'll have to limit shifts to
six hours at a time, but otherwise...

29:23.930 --> 29:26.265
The dosimetrists
should be checking regularly.

29:27.391 --> 29:30.436
Have them use
the good meter from the safe.

29:31.771 --> 29:32.772
Right.

29:33.814 --> 29:35.232
I'll call Maryin.

29:36.442 --> 29:38.861
Have them wake up the local
Executive Committee.

29:38.945 --> 29:40.321
There'll be orders coming down.

29:46.535 --> 29:47.536
Here.

29:48.079 --> 29:50.623
Sure? Okay.

29:53.960 --> 29:55.419
What do you think makes the colors?

29:55.503 --> 29:56.504
Oh.

29:57.171 --> 30:00.341
- It's the fuel, for sure.
- "It's the fuel, for sure."

30:00.716 --> 30:03.761
What do you know about it?
You clean floors at a train station.

30:04.136 --> 30:05.846
My friend, Yuri,
works at the power plant.

30:05.930 --> 30:07.056
He says it runs cold.

30:07.598 --> 30:09.308
No gas, no fire. Just atoms.

30:10.351 --> 30:12.561
Yuri says the only thing is,
you can't walk right up to the fuel.

30:12.979 --> 30:15.690
If you do, a glass of vodka
an hour for four hours.

30:16.482 --> 30:18.109
Isn't Yuri a plumber?

30:18.776 --> 30:20.903
At the nuclear power plant, yeah.

30:27.451 --> 30:28.869
Well, it is beautiful.

30:30.246 --> 30:31.247
Yeah.

32:23.192 --> 32:24.610
Do you have a cigarette?

32:50.594 --> 32:51.804
Do you need help?

32:58.769 --> 32:59.770
It's over.

34:05.127 --> 34:06.795
We've done all we can
from the perimeter.

34:06.879 --> 34:08.547
We need to start making
our way to the roof.

34:15.721 --> 34:16.722
Vasily!

34:17.389 --> 34:18.432
You've got to put it out.

34:22.478 --> 34:25.272
That's enough, comrades.
We're pushing ahead.

34:31.153 --> 34:32.154
Come on, boys.

34:38.744 --> 34:40.329
Vasily,
it's just past, straight up.

34:40.788 --> 34:42.373
All the way up, all the way in.

34:44.458 --> 34:45.459
Come on!

34:58.222 --> 34:59.890
Yeah. Going in now.

35:47.896 --> 35:49.064
What about the auxiliary?

35:50.065 --> 35:52.860
The pumps are gone, electrical's gone.

35:53.902 --> 35:54.903
The core?

35:55.362 --> 35:57.323
I didn't go in there, and I won't.

35:59.491 --> 36:00.534
I think it's time we faced...

36:00.659 --> 36:01.910
No, we have to get water into
the core.

36:01.994 --> 36:03.078
Otherwise, there'll be a meltdown.

36:04.163 --> 36:05.581
We have to open the valves.

36:05.664 --> 36:07.666
- Sasha...
- What do you want, Boris?

36:07.750 --> 36:09.752
If it's true, then we're dead.
A million people are dead.

36:10.002 --> 36:11.128
Is that what you need to hear?

36:13.589 --> 36:15.174
We have to open the valves.

36:15.466 --> 36:16.759
- By hand.
- By hand?

36:18.552 --> 36:20.262
The number of valves,
the amount of time to turn them,

36:20.346 --> 36:21.972
you're talking about hours in there!

36:22.056 --> 36:23.640
- Then help us.
- Help you do what?

36:24.099 --> 36:26.477
Pump water into a ditch?
There's nothing there!

36:36.362 --> 36:37.571
Leonid, I'm begging you.

36:51.418 --> 36:52.669
Watch the panel while we're gone.

36:53.212 --> 36:54.338
It's not working.

36:55.631 --> 36:56.632
Just watch it.

37:19.405 --> 37:21.115
I guess we know why
they called us in early.

37:21.573 --> 37:23.117
Is anyone
saying what happened?

37:23.784 --> 37:25.869
They were running
the safety test on the turbines,

37:26.245 --> 37:27.996
blew the control system tank.

37:29.373 --> 37:30.499
It doesn't make sense to me either.

37:32.543 --> 37:33.627
What about sabotage?

37:34.753 --> 37:35.754
A bomb?

37:37.005 --> 37:38.048
Sitnikov!

37:38.590 --> 37:40.843
Bryukhanov wants us to use
the good dosimeter,

37:40.926 --> 37:43.637
but it's in the safe,
and we can't find the key.

37:43.720 --> 37:45.681
It's in Building Two. Hasn't...

37:47.057 --> 37:48.100
Follow me.

37:59.987 --> 38:01.280
Gentlemen, welcome.

38:01.655 --> 38:04.908
Please, uh, find a seat.
Plenty of room.

38:05.784 --> 38:07.744
I apologize for the lateness
of the hour.

38:08.579 --> 38:12.207
Rest assured,
we are all very safe down here.

38:12.666 --> 38:15.502
We built this shelter
to withstand a nuclear attack

38:15.586 --> 38:18.464
by the Americans,
so, I think we'll be fine.

38:20.424 --> 38:22.885
Um, as you can see,
we have experienced an accident.

38:22.968 --> 38:25.596
A large control tank malfunctioned,

38:25.679 --> 38:29.600
damaging reactor Building Four
and starting a fire.

38:29.683 --> 38:33.228
Now, I have spoken directly
to Deputy Secretary Maryin.

38:33.312 --> 38:35.439
Maryin spoke
to Deputy Chief Frolyshev,

38:35.731 --> 38:38.567
Frolyshev to Central Committee
member Dolgikh,

38:38.984 --> 38:42.154
and Dolgikh to
General Secretary Gorbachev.

38:42.738 --> 38:43.739
Now...

38:45.407 --> 38:49.661
Because the Central Committee
has the greatest respect

38:49.745 --> 38:53.290
for the work of the Pripyat
Executive Committee,

38:53.665 --> 38:57.169
they have asked me to brief you
on matters as they stand, so...

38:59.171 --> 39:00.714
First, the accident...

39:00.797 --> 39:02.758
It's well under control.

39:03.467 --> 39:08.347
And second, because the efforts
of the Soviet nuclear industry

39:08.430 --> 39:11.808
are considered key State secrets,
it is important

39:12.142 --> 39:17.439
that we ensure that this incident
has no adverse consequences.

39:17.898 --> 39:19.441
Now, to prevent a panic,

39:20.192 --> 39:21.860
the Central Committee have ordered

39:21.944 --> 39:24.530
a detachment of military police
to Pripyat.

39:24.821 --> 39:26.198
How large of a detachment?

39:27.991 --> 39:29.785
Between 2,000 and 4,000 men.

39:32.371 --> 39:33.789
What's really going on here?

39:34.665 --> 39:36.083
How dangerous is this?

39:36.792 --> 39:40.128
There's mild radiation,
but it's limited to the plant itself.

39:40.379 --> 39:42.297
- No, it isn't.
- Excuse me?

39:43.549 --> 39:46.093
You saw men outside vomiting.

39:47.511 --> 39:48.762
You saw men with burns.

39:50.347 --> 39:52.015
There's more radiation
than they're saying.

39:52.849 --> 39:54.851
We have wives here, we have children.

39:55.185 --> 39:57.563
I say we evacuate the town.

39:58.522 --> 39:59.523
Gentlemen...

39:59.856 --> 40:03.235
Please... Please! My wife is here.

40:04.069 --> 40:07.281
Do you think I would keep her
in Pripyat if it wasn't safe?

40:07.656 --> 40:11.118
Bryukhanov, the air is glowing.

40:11.285 --> 40:12.286
The Cherenkov effect.

40:13.412 --> 40:16.290
Completely normal phenomenon.
It can happen with minimal radiation.

40:26.800 --> 40:30.137
I wonder how many of you
know the name of this place.

40:33.098 --> 40:35.434
We all call it "Chernobyl," of course.

40:37.227 --> 40:38.854
What is its real name?

40:40.272 --> 40:43.692
The Vladimir I. Lenin
Nuclear Power Station.

40:44.776 --> 40:45.944
Exactly.

40:48.238 --> 40:51.283
Vladimir I. Lenin.

40:59.041 --> 41:02.127
And how proud he would be
of you all tonight.

41:03.754 --> 41:05.756
Especially you, young man,

41:07.174 --> 41:09.426
and the passion you have
for the people.

41:10.886 --> 41:14.431
For is that not the sole purpose
of the apparatus of the State?

41:16.683 --> 41:18.226
Sometimes, we forget.

41:19.936 --> 41:21.897
Sometimes, we fall prey to fear.

41:24.524 --> 41:27.611
But our faith in Soviet socialism

41:28.612 --> 41:30.781
will always be rewarded.

41:33.742 --> 41:37.579
Now, the State tells us
the situation here is not dangerous.

41:38.455 --> 41:40.290
Have faith, comrades.

41:42.501 --> 41:45.462
The State tells us
it wants to prevent a panic.

41:45.545 --> 41:46.922
Listen well.

41:50.175 --> 41:54.137
It's true, when the people see
the police, they will be afraid.

41:55.681 --> 41:57.641
But it is my experience

41:58.975 --> 42:01.144
that when the people ask questions

42:01.228 --> 42:03.397
that are not
in their own best interest...

42:04.523 --> 42:08.652
They should simply be told
to keep their minds on their labor,

42:09.736 --> 42:11.905
and leave matters of the State

42:13.031 --> 42:14.199
to the State.

42:16.368 --> 42:17.953
We seal off the city.

42:19.454 --> 42:20.706
No one leaves.

42:21.873 --> 42:23.458
And cut the phone lines.

42:24.292 --> 42:26.503
Contain the spread of misinformation.

42:29.715 --> 42:32.592
That is how we keep the people

42:32.676 --> 42:35.303
from undermining the fruits
of their own labor.

42:38.724 --> 42:39.975
Yes, comrades.

42:41.643 --> 42:45.188
We will all be rewarded
for what we do here tonight.

42:48.066 --> 42:51.445
This is our moment to shine.

43:04.541 --> 43:05.542
Thank you.

43:18.680 --> 43:20.932
Comrade Sitnikov to see
the Chief Engineer.

43:34.196 --> 43:35.197
Well?

43:42.078 --> 43:45.123
I sent my dosimetrists
into the reactor building.

43:47.042 --> 43:48.293
The large dosimeter from the safe,

43:48.376 --> 43:50.128
the one with
the 1,000-roentgen capacity...

43:50.212 --> 43:51.213
What was the number?

43:54.758 --> 43:56.009
There was none.

43:56.384 --> 43:58.512
The meter burned out
the second it was turned on.

43:59.721 --> 44:00.722
It's typical.

44:00.806 --> 44:01.890
See, this is what Moscow does.

44:01.973 --> 44:04.893
Sends us shit equipment,
then wonders why things go wrong.

44:04.976 --> 44:08.522
We found another dosimeter,
from the military fire department.

44:09.481 --> 44:11.942
It only goes to 200 roentgen,
but it's better than the small ones.

44:12.025 --> 44:13.026
And?

44:14.361 --> 44:15.695
It maxed out.

44:16.613 --> 44:17.781
Two-hundred roentgen.

44:20.742 --> 44:22.160
What game are you playing?

44:22.661 --> 44:23.829
No, I...

44:24.454 --> 44:26.540
I asked him.
He took multiple measurements.

44:26.873 --> 44:27.916
He's my best man.

44:28.250 --> 44:30.627
It's another faulty meter.
You're wasting our time.

44:30.961 --> 44:32.754
I checked the meter
against the control.

44:32.838 --> 44:35.048
What's wrong with you?
How'd you get that number

44:35.131 --> 44:37.050
from feedwater leaking
from a blown tank?

44:40.345 --> 44:41.346
You don't.

44:41.972 --> 44:43.765
Then what the fuck
are you talking about?

44:48.270 --> 44:49.271
I...

44:52.148 --> 44:54.901
I walked around the exterior
of Building Four.

44:56.736 --> 44:59.489
I think there's graphite
on the ground in the rubble.

45:00.907 --> 45:02.284
You didn't see graphite.

45:03.618 --> 45:04.828
- I did.
- You didn't.

45:06.538 --> 45:09.791
You didn't! Because it's not there!

45:11.418 --> 45:12.419
What?

45:13.044 --> 45:15.171
Are you suggesting the core...

45:15.422 --> 45:17.632
What, exploded?

45:20.427 --> 45:21.428
Yes.

45:30.437 --> 45:31.438
Sitnikov.

45:32.606 --> 45:34.441
You're a nuclear engineer. So am I.

45:35.358 --> 45:40.572
So please tell me how
an RBMK reactor core explodes.

45:41.698 --> 45:44.826
Not a meltdown, an explosion.

45:45.827 --> 45:47.037
I'd love to know.

45:48.079 --> 45:49.080
I can't.

45:50.332 --> 45:51.333
Are you stupid?

45:53.084 --> 45:54.085
No.

45:54.419 --> 45:55.545
Then why can't you?

45:57.380 --> 45:58.381
I...

46:00.926 --> 46:03.094
I don't see how it could explode...

46:05.347 --> 46:06.348
But it did.

46:06.431 --> 46:07.432
Enough!

46:08.016 --> 46:09.684
I'll go up to the vent block roof.

46:09.768 --> 46:12.437
From there, you can look right
down into reactor Building Four.

46:12.646 --> 46:13.772
I'll see it with my own...

46:15.774 --> 46:16.900
My own eyes.

46:22.656 --> 46:23.865
I apologize.

46:25.867 --> 46:27.243
Guards! Guards!

46:28.662 --> 46:31.623
Get him to a medic, or the hospital!
Whatever he needs!

46:48.264 --> 46:51.017
The feedwater.
Been around it all night.

46:53.728 --> 46:54.729
You go, then.

46:58.483 --> 46:59.484
What?

46:59.776 --> 47:02.487
Go to the vent block roof
and report back what you see.

47:02.570 --> 47:03.571
No.

47:07.534 --> 47:08.994
No, I won't do that.

47:09.995 --> 47:11.246
Of course you will.

47:16.418 --> 47:17.460
You'll be fine.

47:18.378 --> 47:19.379
You'll see.

47:20.588 --> 47:21.589
Come on.

48:03.965 --> 48:04.966
Okay.

48:06.926 --> 48:07.969
Let's begin.

48:16.478 --> 48:17.479
Leonid.

48:21.816 --> 48:22.817
Leonid.

48:31.534 --> 48:32.619
It's all the way, okay?

48:33.661 --> 48:35.080
All the way open.

48:44.672 --> 48:45.673
I'm sorry.

48:49.761 --> 48:51.304
There's nothing to be sorry for.

48:52.013 --> 48:54.766
I told you. We did nothing wrong.

48:57.685 --> 48:58.812
But we did.

52:00.952 --> 52:02.787
Get everyone
in the infirmary up there.

52:47.373 --> 52:48.374
Hello?

52:48.458 --> 52:50.585
- Valery Legasov?
- -Yes.

52:50.668 --> 52:53.171
You are the Legasov who is
the First Deputy Director

52:53.254 --> 52:55.757
of the Kurchatov Institute
of Atomic Energy?

52:55.840 --> 52:58.009
- I am. Who am I speaking...
- This is Boris Shcherbina,

52:58.426 --> 53:00.428
Deputy Chairman of
the Council of Ministers

53:00.511 --> 53:02.597
and head of the Bureau
for Fuel and Energy.

53:03.514 --> 53:06.809
There's been an accident
at the Chernobyl nuclear power plant.

53:07.810 --> 53:08.811
How bad is it?

53:09.479 --> 53:11.522
No, no need to panic.
There was a fire.

53:11.606 --> 53:14.400
It's mostly put out.
The system control tank exploded.

53:14.692 --> 53:16.361
"Control system tank."

53:16.694 --> 53:17.779
And the core?

53:18.196 --> 53:20.531
We've ordered them
to continuously pump water.

53:21.240 --> 53:23.618
Yes, I see. Any contamination?

53:24.118 --> 53:26.788
It's mild. The plant manager,
Bryukhanov, is reporting

53:26.871 --> 53:28.539
3.6 roentgen per hour.

53:28.623 --> 53:30.708
That's actually significant.
You should evacuate the...

53:30.792 --> 53:34.212
You're an expert on
RBMK reactors, correct?

53:35.588 --> 53:38.216
- Yes. I've studied...
- General Secretary Gorbachev

53:38.299 --> 53:40.968
has appointed a committee
to manage the accident.

53:41.469 --> 53:42.470
You're on it.

53:43.429 --> 53:45.181
We'll convene at 2:00 this afternoon.

53:45.681 --> 53:48.810
That late? Forgive me,
but don't you think,

53:48.893 --> 53:50.686
given the amount of radiation,
that it would be...

53:50.770 --> 53:53.898
Legasov, you're on this committee
to answer direct questions

53:53.981 --> 53:56.192
about the function of an RBMK reactor,

53:56.359 --> 53:59.445
if they should happen to arise.
Nothing else,

53:59.654 --> 54:01.739
certainly not policy.
Do you understand?

54:02.323 --> 54:04.409
Yes, of course. I didn't mean to...
